BOOK:Displacement_Constraints
NUMBER: 1 CONDITION: Point-Constraints
CONDTYPE: over points
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: Use this condition to prescribe the displacement of selected points.\nEvery marked flag will prescribe the movement for that degree of freedom.\nThe values fields permmit to set a prescribed displacementfor that degree.\nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the displacements.
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: X_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-X,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-X,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-X#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
QUESTION: Y_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-Y,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-Y,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-Y#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
QUESTION: Z_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-Z,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-Z,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-Z#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 2 CONDITION: Linear-Constraints
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: Use this condition to prescribe the displacement of all the nodes that belong to the line.\nEvery marked flag will prescribe the movement for that degree of freedom.\nThe values fields permmit to set a prescribed displacement for that degree.\nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the displacements.
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: X_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-X,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-X,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-X#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
QUESTION: Y_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-Y,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-Y,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-Y#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
QUESTION: Z_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-Z,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-Z,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-Z#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 3 CONDITION: Surface-Constraints
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: X_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-X,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-X,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-X#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
QUESTION: Y_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-Y,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-Y,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-Y#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
QUESTION: Z_Constraint:#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Displacement-Z,0.0m)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Displacement-Z,0.0m)
QUESTION: Displacement-Z#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000m
END CONDITION
BOOK:Elastic_Constraints
NUMBER: 4 CONDITION: Point-Elast._Constraints
CONDTYPE: over points
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
CANREPEAT: yes
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: Kx:#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000N/m
QUESTION: Ky:#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000N/m
QUESTION: Kz:#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.000N/m
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 5 CONDITION: Linear-Elast._Constraints
CONDTYPE: over lines
