BOOK:Loads
NUMBER: 7 CONDITION: Point-Load
CONDTYPE: over points
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: A force applied to the selected points of the model. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N) for the forces.
QUESTION: X-Force#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0N
QUESTION: Y-Force#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0N
QUESTION: Z-Force#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0N
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 8 CONDITION: Global_Proyected_Pressure
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
HELP: A pressure load over the contour of the solid given in global axes and projected as if the area of the contour was the projected area over the pressure vector. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m2) for the pressures.
QUESTION: X_Pressure#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0N/m^2
QUESTION: Y_Pressure#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0N/m^2
QUESTION: Z_Pressure#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0N/m^2
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 9 CONDITION: Uniform_Pressure
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
HELP: HELP: A pressure load over the contour of the solid given in global axes. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m2) for the pressures.
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(GLOBAL,Automatic)
VALUE: GLOBAL
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
