NUMBER: 10 CONDITION: Trapezoidal-Pressure
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
HELP: This load is similar to that of 'Uniform_Pressure' but its intensity changes depending on the point where it is applied. The two points define an imaginary line in the space. For every point of the volume contour  where the load is applied, it is possible to project this point on the imaginary line and interpolate the values related to these points depending on where it is projected. \nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the points\n\t(N/m2) for the pressures.
TITLE: Position
QUESTION: X_point_1#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0m
QUESTION: Y_point_1#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0m
QUESTION: Z_point_1#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0m
QUESTION: X_point_2#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0m
QUESTION: Y_point_2#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0m
QUESTION: Z_point_2#UNITS#
VALUE: 0.0m
TITLE: Pressures
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(GLOBAL,Automatic)
VALUE: GLOBAL
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
